# Phase discipline

Read [docs/master-spec.md](docs/master-spec.md) and the current phase doc before changing code.

Work only on the current phase. Phase 1 through Phase 11 are complete. See [docs/phase-11.md](docs/phase-11.md). Next is scale-in (Phase 12). Do not write or start Phase 12 until Click asks.

Feature work happens on `develop`. Merge to `main` only when the user is ready for production.

Phase 11 is the first managing playbook. Type `dca` on the desk. Same `futures_*` ledger and `runFuturesCommand`. The app owns orders and exits. Signals only arm. Stacked playbooks, one per contract and side. Do not add a Fly.io worker. Do not call private exchange APIs from the browser. Paper accounts still use the in-app ledger.

Do not create later-phase tables or speculative architecture. Do not start scale-in, Hyperliquid, MEXC, or onboarding wizard refine until Click asks. Hyperliquid is planned in [docs/phase-hyperliquid.md](docs/phase-hyperliquid.md) and is **on hold**. See [docs/phase-onboarding.md](docs/phase-onboarding.md).

Keep dependencies minimal. Prefer the simplest solution that satisfies the current phase.

Stop at the end of the phase. After acceptance criteria pass, report results and wait for instruction.
